d['law_screen']='The actual McConnell public holdings, final Greenville and Virginia completeness copies and the final clean public-law model receipt establish no change to the frozen review-channel, warning, noncounting or independent improper-conversion grounds. Election-specific review routes do not rewrite the actual section 2255 classification question; notice cannot cure an undefined substantive command, but Castro concerns an existing procedural choice and its consequence. Virginia’s sovereign-acquiescence inquiry supplies no informed selection of this procedural vehicle. The now-durable December 11 Deaton public holding was also screened: its distinct statutory delegation, channel protection, preserved Manual issue and equitable restoration create no section 2255 conversion rule, authorization act or waiver premise. The final Castro form and every frozen join therefore remain unchanged. Scalia and Thomas’s original provisional affirmative merits joins are superseded by their frozen reconciliation; neither the later receipt’s shorthand nor assembly restores them.'
d['affected_later']='After fixing Castro’s three holdings, its actual rule was compared with the five completed later public decisions. Rancho Viejo’s wildlife-taking mechanism and existing-record remand, Lomont’s official-injury and unconditional-refusal rules, Environmental Defense Center’s own-discharge alternative and operational-information grounds, ACLU of New Jersey’s custody-information delegation and separately justified APA exceptions, and West Virginia v. HHS’s conditional funding and genuine-choice inquiry do not depend on counting an unwarned pro se conversion or treating an antecedent-classification judgment as a circuit authorization act. Castro’s federal procedural supervision does not impose its three warnings on those unrelated administrative choices. No necessary later premise, remedy or preserved component is displaced. Their holdings were used only for this consequence screen and supplied no present merits rule.'
